  "notes": "A self-contained jam-band-adjacent ensemble inside country radio — acoustic-led, harmony-rich, with genuine improvisation. The defining palette fact is authored as a melodic one because the entry states it that way: \"acoustic guitar is the lead instrument, not a bed,\" so the melody's timbre hint and the counter's answer weighting both sit on the acoustic string set rather than on steel. Drums are \"a light, dry kit with a strong shaker/tambourine 8th layer and cross-stick verses; the jam cuts open into extended instrumental vamps where the kit rides the hat,\" hence a continuous hat with a modest fill count and the shaker/tambourine lanes carrying more density than the kit. Harmony is \"I–IV–V and I–V–vi–IV with ii–V folk turnarounds; the island cuts sit on a I–IV vamp,\" and the folk/Celtic modal colour the entry names is the mixolydian weight. The bass is \"root-fifth with walking motion; occasional upright.\" The arrangement is the entry's other real structural claim — \"extended instrumental (16–32 bars, traded)\" — so the bridge slot is the longest in this batch. ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: medium-high); the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF] and the entry notes the debut hit's 170 reading folds to ~85. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the perc density, the humanize values and the counter ratio.",
